            <subFactors xsi:type="dssmm:LeafFactor" FactorID="195128" Name="Multiple calendars" Descr="Multiple calendars may be useful for different accounting scenarios. For example, different financial entities may need separate fiscal calendars--one set of books might require a quarterly calendar while another would require a different term. If a merger results in two financial entities that have different fiscal calendars, the accounting system will need to maintain both calendars and normalize the data (Q2 for Entity A is equal to Q3 for Entity B). This may also be useful for what-if scenarios." GW="3.6E-5" LW="0.022727" Hierarchy="1.5.1.5" MasterFactorID="195128">
